      {
        "id": 177326,
        "name": "MigrantP",
        "username": "MigrantP",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/migrantp/{size}/1921_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-06-09T16:35:07.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Due to what actually happens, we don't care about the non-condition cards. This makes the odds of it happening a lot higher!</p><p>Here are the condition cards:</p><p>An Unwise Wager (1)</p><p>Losing to the Odds (1)</p><p>Not All He Seems (1)</p><p>Playing Dice With the Cosmos (1)</p><p>The New Deal (1)</p><p>Wagelings (4)</p><p>Who Are You Fighting? (1)</p><p>So there are actually only 10 (TEN!) condition cards!</p><p>There's a 4 in 10 chance he plays a Wageling first. P = (4/10) = 40% chance</p><p>There's a 3 in 9 chance he also plays a second one. P = (3/9) * (4/10) ~= 13.33% chance</p><p>There's a 2 in 8 chance he also plays a third one. P = (2/8) * (3/9) * (4/10) ~= 3.33% chance</p><p>There's a 1 in 7 chance he also plays a fourth one. P = (1/7) *&nbsp;(2/8) * (3/9) * (4/10)&nbsp;~=&nbsp;0.476% chance</p><p>So the actual odds are 1 in 30 for H=3, and 1 in 210 for H=4. Not that rare at all!</p>",
