        "created_at": "2016-06-09T18:07:29.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"MigrantP\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/migrantp/48/1921_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> MigrantP:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Due to what actually happens, we don't care about the non-condition cards. This makes the odds of it happening a lot higher!Here are the condition cards:An Unwise Wager (1)Losing to the Odds (1)Not All He Seems (1)Playing Dice With the Cosmos (1)The New Deal (1)Wagelings (4)Who Are You Fighting? (1)So there are actually only 10 (TEN!) condition cards!There's a 4 in 10 chance he plays a Wageling first. P = (4/10) = 40% chanceThere's a 3 in 9 chance he also plays a second one. P = (3/9) * (4/10) ~= 13.33% chanceThere's a 2 in 8 chance he also plays a third one. P = (2/8) * (3/9) * (4/10) ~= 3.33% chanceThere's a 1 in 7 chance he also plays a fourth one. P = (1/7) *&nbsp;(2/8) * (3/9) * (4/10)&nbsp;~=&nbsp;0.476% chanceSo the actual odds are 1 in 30 for H=3, and 1 in 210 for H=4. Not that rare at all!</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Ouch.</p>",
